	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Thousand Needles is a great canyon of red stone south of {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}. Its floor is dry and dusty, and from it rise hundreds of narrow spires of rock, so tall and thin that travellers named the whole land after them. The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} reach it by the {link:the-great-lift}Great Lift{/link} on its northern rim, and from the mesas of {link:freewind-post}Freewind Post{/link} they keep watch over the canyon. To the east the stone gives way to the {link:the-shimmering-flats}Shimmering Flats{/link}, a blinding plain of salt where goblins and gnomes race machines of their own making. Wind serpents coil among the needles, wyverns nest on the western heights, and harpies scream in the southern canyons. It is a beautiful country, and a dangerous one.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records how the needles came to stand as they do, nor when the {link:the-shimmering-flats}Shimmering Flats{/link} became a desert of salt. The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} have walked these canyons for generations, and the {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} hunted them here as they hunted them across all the plains of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. Scholars who come to the Flats remark that the border between the green woods of {link:feralas}Feralas{/link} and the dry stone of the Needles is strangely sharp, as if some old magic had drawn it. None of them can say what that magic was.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} of {link:freewind-post}Freewind Post{/link} hold the heart of the canyon, but they hold little else. The Galak {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} raid their caravans from {link:splithoof-crag}Splithoof Crag{/link} and {link:camp-e-thok}Camp E'thok{/link}, and they have sworn to kill any tauren who dares to hunt in the west. On the {link:darkcloud-pinnacle}Darkcloud Pinnacle{/link}, warriors of the {link:grimtotem-clan}Grimtotem Clan{/link} guard the burial ground of their dead and receive strangers who come and go in secret. Freewind Post watches them closely and trusts them less each season.

In the east, the {link:the-shimmering-flats}Shimmering Flats{/link} have become the stage of a long contest. At {link:mirage-raceway}the Mirage Raceway{/link}, a goblin team and a gnomish team race their rocket cars across the salt, and half the rogues and dreamers of the world come to watch and wager. South of the track, dwarves of the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} dug into the earth at the {link:the-rustmaul-dig-site}Rustmaul Dig Site{/link}, and something dug back: a swarm of great insects that the {link:horde}Horde{/link} now calls the silithid. On the northern rim, near the lift, the {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} keep the thorn warren of {link:razorfen-downs}Razorfen Downs{/link}, and robed cultists have been seen on the trails nearby.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:tauren}tauren{/link}.{/b} Braves, hunters and shamans hold {link:freewind-post}Freewind Post{/link} and the small hunting camp of {link:whitereach-post}Whitereach Post{/link}.
• {b}The Grimtotem.{/b} A tauren clan apart, holding the {link:darkcloud-pinnacle}Darkcloud Pinnacle{/link} and distrusting every other tribe.
• {b}The Galak {link:centaurs}centaur{/link}.{/b} Raiders who hold {link:splithoof-crag}Splithoof Crag{/link} and {link:camp-e-thok}Camp E'thok{/link} and war on the tauren.
• {b}The goblins and gnomes of {link:mirage-raceway}the Mirage Raceway{/link}.{/b} Mechanics, pilots, bookmakers and hangers-on.
• {b}The harpies.{/b} The Screeching harpies nest in the Screeching Canyon and in the {link:roguefeather-den}Roguefeather Den{/link}.
• {b}The silithid.{/b} Insects that swarm out of the earth beneath the {link:the-rustmaul-dig-site}Rustmaul Dig Site{/link}.
• {b}The beasts.{/b} Wind serpents, wyverns, cougars, hyenas, basilisks, scorpids and the great tortoises of the salt.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Wandering Years.{/b} The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} tribes crossed these canyons on their long wanderings, hunted by the {link:centaurs}centaur{/link}. Many tauren of {link:freewind-post}Freewind Post{/link} still remember those days.
• {b}The Claiming of Mulgore.{/b} When {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne Bloodhoof{/link} led his people to {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link} with the help of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, the tauren grew strong enough to return to the Needles. No chronicle records when they raised Freewind Post or the {link:the-great-lift}Great Lift{/link}.
• {b}The Coming of the Racers.{/b} Goblins and gnomes found in the {link:the-shimmering-flats}Shimmering Flats{/link} the flattest ground in {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, and they built a race track upon it.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The Galak grow bolder, {link:grimtotem-clan}the Grimtotem{/link} keep secrets, and the silithid have come up out of the earth.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Needles",
			text = [=[• The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} of {link:whitereach-post}Whitereach Post{/link} know a legend of {link:arikara}Arikara{/link}, a serpent of vengeance who rises from the sacred fire of the {link:darkcloud-pinnacle}Darkcloud Pinnacle{/link} against those who have done heinous deeds. Most thought it only a legend.
• The Galak guard a relic from the days when the first {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} were born, kept in a cavern behind a flame that never goes out.
• A hyena the tauren call {link:steelsnap}Steelsnap{/link} gathers other hyenas about him and spreads fear among the gentler beasts of the canyon.
• The pit crews of {link:mirage-raceway}the Mirage Raceway{/link} say that every stretch of {link:the-shimmering-flats}the Flats{/link} is scattered with the wreckage of rocket cars, and that a careful scavenger can make a living from it.]=],
		},
	},
})

